Sure, that’s really easy!  In C and many other programming languages, you can use a loop to repeat a block of code a specified number of times.  Here’s an example with a loop that displays the numbers from 1 to 10:

for (i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    printf("The number is %d\n", i);
}

This loop will display the numbers 1 through 10, one by one.  You can add as many conditions as you want inside the loop, like this:

for (i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        continue;  // Skip this number
    }

    printf("The number is %d\n", i);
}

In this example, we check if the number is even.  If it’s even, we skip it by continuing to the next iteration of the loop.  The loop will only print the numbers that are odd.

